// scripts/** is excluded from the main tsconfig, so `tsc --noEmit` reports a
// clean tree while every script that writes to the production database goes
// unchecked. On 2026-08-30 that let two broken scripts ship in consecutive
// commits — an undefined identifier in enrich-repos.ts (which writes repo
// grades to prod) and a missing import in an eval probe — with vitest, the
// main tsc, and a full CI run all green.
//
// This config type-checks them. It cannot simply be folded into the main
// tsconfig: Next builds from that one, and pulling ~200 node-side scripts into
// the app's program changes what the build compiles. Kept separate, run by its
// own guard (scripts/check-scripts-types.ts).
{
	"extends": "./tsconfig.json",
	"include": ["scripts/**/*.ts", "src/**/*.ts", "src/**/*.tsx"],
	"exclude": ["node_modules", "scout-mcp/**", "api-client/**"]
}
